                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "i love point and click adventures and i love clowns... but i did not like this game. \n\ni found it boring, i don't understand the ending or the plot leading up to it. the ending felt very unsatisfying, what is going on?? and i thought my game crashed because when i got to the ending it just froze on that screen for like 30 seconds and then jumped to the credits.\n\ni found some of the puzzles frankly not straightforward at all. i understand the desire to have the game not have direct communication with words, but i literally had to look up a walkthrough in order to get through multiple major parts of the game because of how incomprehensible it was. the pictures of locations that the people show to \"communicate\" are very crunchy and hard to read, so i just ended up wandering around the huge map repeatedly trying to find how to proceed. plus, if you don't complete certain tasks before certain milestones, you literally cannot come back and do those tasks.\n\ni felt like the click detection when trying to do certain actions was not good and i often had to move the characters in order to complete an action because the characters blocked the window to click. the fast travel function leaves much to be desired. i have no idea how to even do some of the optional side quests, i don't know where to start, and i frankly don't care to waste more time to go back. i don't even understand the DLC, it looks like almost nothing. you can just hug two of the people without doing anything.\n\ni also think the game should have warnings for flashing. the ending has an unskippable portion where the screen is flashing between black and not black and it hurt my eyes.\n\ni do not recommend this game.",
